---

# [OBLIGATORY] Declare valid devices metadata
# - id: device udid: the Identifier of Xcode, Window -> Devices and Simulators (`adb devices` for Android, `xcrun simctl list devices` for an iOS simulator)
#   name: device name as it will be registered in STF
#   location: [optional] clarified device location for ease of device management (an underscore will be added automatically before the value)
#   id, name and location: letters, digits, '_', '.' and '-', the first one a letter or a digit (the spaces of a name become '_');
#     they are the names of the containers, a wireless Android device at ip:port has the address in address
#   appium_port: unique port value for sharing appium services from the container to outside selenium hub
#   adb_port: USB Android: the port of the host forwarded to the device, unique on the host (see connection)
#   connect_port: [optional] Android: the remote debug port of STF (adb connect), the second port of min_port-max_port
#     by default; out of the range it is published too. Unique on the host, and among the hosts for the adb relay of
#     mcloud (README.md#device-hosts-in-a-private-network). Not a port of MCloud on the same machine.
#   min_port and max_port: unique range of ports per device for system STF purposes: Android needs 4 ports besides
#     connect_port (5 with connect_port inside the range), iOS uses the first one (the screen); 6 in the examples.
#     The MCloud server reaches them on STF_PROVIDER_HOST (the screens through stf-proxy); adb connect of the remote
#     debug reaches them directly or through the adb relay of mcloud (REMOTE_CONNECT_HOST, ADB_RELAY=true).
#   connection: [optional] how the connector container reaches the device, usb by default. Docker of macOS has no USB:
#     the connectors take the devices from the host, but every device command comes from the containers.
#     usb       - plugged into the Mac: iOS over usbmuxd of the host (the connector installs and starts WebDriverAgent),
#                 Android over the adb server of the host (a launch agent, brew install android-platform-tools):
#                 adb_port is the port of the host forwarded to the device, unique on the host
#     wireless  - over the network: iOS / Apple TV paired with the Mac (usbmuxd of the host knows it), Android over
#                 adb connect to address (the id by default, port 5555 unless given)
#     android-sim - Android: an emulator started outside the farm, address is its adb address: an AVD of the Mac
#                 is host.docker.internal:5555 (5557, ... for the next ones), a container Android or Genymotion of the network
#     ios-sim   - an iOS / tvOS simulator of the Mac, id is its UDID (xcrun simctl list devices): the connector
#                 boots it and starts WebDriverAgent over ssh (Remote Login must be on), wda_port (and mjpeg_port,
#                 wda_port + 1 by default) are its unique ports on the host, wda_file the simulator build of WDA
#                 (a .app folder or its .zip, WDA_SIMULATOR_FILE by default)
#     proxy     - iOS: WebDriverAgent started by another tool and published on address (wda_port, mjpeg_port: 8100, 8101)
#   address, wda_port and mjpeg_port: [optional] see connection
#   wda_file and wda_bundleid: [optional] device specific overrides of WDA_FILE and WDA_BUNDLEID

devices:
  - id: d6afc6b3a65584ca0813eb8957c6479b9b6ebb11
    os: ios
    name: iPhone_8_Plus
    location: location_1
    appium_port: 7431
    min_port: 7435
    max_port: 7440
